SUBENT        C3135001   20260717   20261014   20261014       C259
BIB                 11         46
TITLE      Measurement of high-energy resonances in 22Ne through
           inverse kinematics
AUTHOR     (B.Greaves,D.Mucher,S.Gillespie,T.Drake,L.Atar,
           A.Babu,F.Barrett,N.Bernier,S.S.Bhattacharjee,
           V.Bildstein,R.Caballero-Folch,W.N.Catford,A.Chester,
           C.Aa.Diget,A.Garnsworthy,G.Hackman,E.Kasanda,
           A.M.Laird,B.Olaizola,N.A.Orr,T.Rockman,Y.Saito,
           P.Siuryte,A.Spyrou,C.E.Svensson,R.Umashankar)
REFERENCE  (J,PR/C,113,065806,2026)
           #doi:10.1103/h5h1-xrj2
INSTITUTE  (1CANGUE,2ITYPAD,2GERKLN,1CANTMF,1USAMSU,1CANTOR,
           3AULCBR,1CANUBC,2SPNAUT,2UK SUR,2UK YRK,1CANSFU,
           2SWTUBE,2SPNIEM,2FR CAE,2NEDDEL)
           (1CANCAN) Department of Physics and Astronomy,
           University of Calgary, Calgary, Alberta T2N 1N4, Canada
FACILITY   (CYCLO,1CANTMF) The postaccelerated Isotope Separator
           and Accelerator (ISAC) II facility at TRIUMF.
INC-SPECT  The microwave cusp ion source (MWIS) at the Off-Line
           Ion Source (OLIS) was used to produce a beam of 21Ne
           from a gas source, which was accelerated with the
           superconducting linear accelerator (SC-LINAC) to
           deliver a 165 MeV beam with an intensity of 5*10**8
           particles per second (pps).
DETECTOR   (SI,HPGE,SPEC) The Silicon Highly segmented Array for
           Reactions and Coulex (SHARC) is a charged-particle
           spectrometer embedded within the target chamber for
           this experiment. In addition, the downstream box
           offers dE-E through a box of backing MSX35
           single-area detectors. Surrounding SHARC, TIGRESS
            (TRIUMF-ISAC Gamma-Ray Escape-Suppressed
           Spectrometer) was used to measure the gamma rays
           emitted from the ejectile 22Ne.
SAMPLE     A 120 microg/cm2 deuterated polyethylene (CD2) target
           at the center of the combined SHARC/TIGRESS
           measurement station.
METHOD     (EDE) A 165 MeV beam of 21Ne was delivered to a
           deuterated polyethylene (CD2) target, resulting in the
           population of an excited 22Ne nucleus and a recoil
           proton. This reaction mechanism was studied with two
           surrounding complementary arrays: SHARC, a segmented
           silicon array for measurement of recoil particles, and
           TIGRESS, a high-purity, segmented germanium clover
           array for measurement and correction of
           Doppler-shifted gamma rays.
STATUS     (APRVD) Approved by B.Greaves on July 30, 2026.
